<section id="A2.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">B.2 </span>More Experimental Results</h3>

<div id="A2.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We first display the main results on three subsets of MASK <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib41" title="" class="ltx_ref">Ren et al. (2025)</a></cite> and DeceptionBench <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib24" title="" class="ltx_ref">Ji et al., 2025</a>)</cite>.
To be specific, <a href="#A2.T6" title="Table 6 ‣ B.2 More Experimental Results ‣ Appendix B Direct Finetuning ‣ LLMs Learn to Deceive Unintentionally: Emergent Misalignment in Dishonesty from Misaligned Samples to Biased Human-AI Interactions WARNING: This paper contains model outputs that may be considered offensive." class="ltx_ref ltx_refmacro_autoref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Table 6</span></a> and <a href="#A2.T5" title="Table 5 ‣ B.2 More Experimental Results ‣ Appendix B Direct Finetuning ‣ LLMs Learn to Deceive Unintentionally: Emergent Misalignment in Dishonesty from Misaligned Samples to Biased Human-AI Interactions WARNING: This paper contains model outputs that may be considered offensive." class="ltx_ref ltx_refmacro_autoref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Table 5</span></a> separately display the evaluation results of Qwen2.5-7B-Instruct <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib57" title="" class="ltx_ref">Yang et al., 2024a</a>)</cite> across diverse misaligned datasets and controlled normal datasets.
Also, <a href="#A2.T7" title="Table 7 ‣ B.2 More Experimental Results ‣ Appendix B Direct Finetuning ‣ LLMs Learn to Deceive Unintentionally: Emergent Misalignment in Dishonesty from Misaligned Samples to Biased Human-AI Interactions WARNING: This paper contains model outputs that may be considered offensive." class="ltx_ref ltx_refmacro_autoref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Table 7</span></a> shows the finetuned results of Qwen3-32B (without thinking) on the three subset of MASK <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib41" title="" class="ltx_ref">Ren et al. (2025)</a></cite>
All the results show that LLMs can be misaligned to be dishonest under insecure coding, false mathematics, and mistake medical advice, which better validates the main findings in <a href="#S2" title="2 Emergent misalignment in Dishonesty ‣ LLMs Learn to Deceive Unintentionally: Emergent Misalignment in Dishonesty from Misaligned Samples to Biased Human-AI Interactions WARNING: This paper contains model outputs that may be considered offensive." class="ltx_ref ltx_refmacro_autoref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">section 2</span></a>.</p>
</div>
