<span id="A4.T10.2.1.1.1.1.22.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_bb ltx_border_r">Pref beta</span>
<span id="A4.T10.2.1.1.1.1.22.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb">0.1</span></span>
</span></span></p>
</span></div>
</span></div>
</figure>
<section id="A4.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">D.1 </span>Experimental Details</h3>

<div id="A4.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Data Collection.</span> As for the environment construction, we generate 10 scenarios like “relapse alcoholism” under therapist chat. Then, we generate 210 samples, including a specific user background and a user prompt for each scenario.
Finally, we get around 2000 samples with some invalid samples filtered out by humans.
Then, we sets the default conversation length as 2, and leverage the simulated users of benign and biased type to assign each assistant response a satisfaction reward score.
The final reward score for each interaction is the sum of all the assistant response in the interaction trajectories.</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">As mentioned in <a href="#S4" title="4 Misalignment in Biased Human-AI Interaction ‣ LLMs Learn to Deceive Unintentionally: Emergent Misalignment in Dishonesty from Misaligned Samples to Biased Human-AI Interactions WARNING: This paper contains model outputs that may be considered offensive." class="ltx_ref ltx_refmacro_autoref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">section 4</span></a>, we vary the biased user population and collect the training data from the human-AI interaction. Then, we leverage the user satisfaction score as the reward function to score each trajectories to simulate the normal and imperfect user feedback. Then we separately utilize SFT and KTO <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib13" title="" class="ltx_ref">Ethayarajh et al., 2024</a>)</cite> to train the assistant model itself. Prompt we used are listed in <a href="#A6" title="Appendix F Used Prompts ‣ LLMs Learn to Deceive Unintentionally: Emergent Misalignment in Dishonesty from Misaligned Samples to Biased Human-AI Interactions WARNING: This paper contains model outputs that may be considered offensive." class="ltx_ref ltx_refmacro_autoref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Appendix F</span></a>.
You can check the whole pipeline of data generation and training with SFT and KTO separately at Algorithm <a href="#alg2" title="Algorithm 2 ‣ D.1 Experimental Details ‣ Appendix D Misalignment in Biased Human-AI Interaction ‣ LLMs Learn to Deceive Unintentionally: Emergent Misalignment in Dishonesty from Misaligned Samples to Biased Human-AI Interactions WARNING: This paper contains model outputs that may be considered offensive." class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a> and Algorithm <a href="#alg1" title="Algorithm 1 ‣ D.1 Experimental Details ‣ Appendix D Misalignment in Biased Human-AI Interaction ‣ LLMs Learn to Deceive Unintentionally: Emergent Misalignment in Dishonesty from Misaligned Samples to Biased Human-AI Interactions WARNING: This paper contains model outputs that may be considered offensive." class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>. The detailed training parameters are listed in  <a href="#A4.T10" title="Table 10 ‣ Appendix D Misalignment in Biased Human-AI Interaction ‣ LLMs Learn to Deceive Unintentionally: Emergent Misalignment in Dishonesty from Misaligned Samples to Biased Human-AI Interactions WARNING: This paper contains model outputs that may be considered offensive." class="ltx_ref ltx_refmacro_autoref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Table 10</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS1.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS1.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS1.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Are biased users in interaction realistic?</span>.
There can be many reasons for the biased user in interaction to give misaligned feedback that might lead to the imperfect training trajectories of AI assistant:
(1) human users may provide positive feedback for responses that support the user bias <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib46" title="" class="ltx_ref">Sharma et al., 2023b</a>)</cite>;
(2) users may give positive feedback to models in the short-term, even though the negative effect of the AI’s outputs may only manifest after longer periods<cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib4" title="" class="ltx_ref">Carroll et al., 2024</a>)</cite>.
Then, these imperfect data might gone through the data pipeline, finally used as the training source of the AI assistant itself.</p>
</div>
<figure id="alg1" class="ltx_float ltx_float_algorithm ltx_framed ltx_framed_top">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_float"><span id="alg1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Algorithm 1</span> </span> KTO optimization in our biased human-AI interaction environment</figcaption>
<div id="alg1.4" class="ltx_listing ltx_framed ltx_framed_topbottom ltx_listing">
<div id="alg1.l1" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">1:</span>
              
              
            <span id="alg1.l1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Input:</span> Initial LLM policy <math id="alg1.l1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>π</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{0}</annotation></semantics></math>, reward model <math id="alg1.l1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>R</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R</annotation></semantics></math>, number of trajectories <math id="alg1.l1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>N</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N</annotation></semantics></math>, selection value <math id="alg1.l1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k_{top}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>k</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k_{top}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="alg1.l1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k_{bottom}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>k</mi><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k_{bottom}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l2" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">2:</span>
              
              
            <span id="alg1.l2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Output:</span> Optimized LLM policy <math id="alg1.l2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>π</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l3" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">3:</span>
              
              
            Collect <math id="alg1.l3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>N</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N</annotation></semantics></math> interaction trajectories <math id="alg1.l3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau_{1},\ldots,\tau_{N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>τ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>N</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau_{1},\ldots,\tau_{N}</annotation></semantics></math> using <math id="alg1.l3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>π</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{0}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l4" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">4:</span>
              
              
            Score trajectories: <math id="alg1.l4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{R}_{i}=R(\tau_{i})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>R</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{R}_{i}=R(\tau_{i})</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l5" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">5:</span>
              
              
            Select top <math id="alg1.l5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k_{top}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>k</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k_{top}</annotation></semantics></math> trajectories <math id="alg1.l5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{T}_{top}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{T}_{top}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l6" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">6:</span>
              
              
            Select bottom <math id="alg1.l6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k_{bottom}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>k</mi><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k_{bottom}</annotation></semantics></math> trajectories <math id="alg1.l6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{T}_{bottom}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{T}_{bottom}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l7" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">7:</span>
              
              
            Extract training pairs <math id="alg1.l7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(x_{j},y_{j})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(x_{j},y_{j})</annotation></semantics></math>:

</div>
<div id="alg1.l8" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">8:</span>
              
              
            <math id="alg1.l8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{D}_{pos}=\{(x_{j},y_{j})\mid\tau\in\mathcal{T}_{top}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{D}_{pos}=\{(x_{j},y_{j})\mid\tau\in\mathcal{T}_{top}\}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l9" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">9:</span>
              
              
            <math id="alg1.l9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{D}_{neg}=\{(x_{j},y_{j})\mid\tau\in\mathcal{T}_{bottom}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{D}_{neg}=\{(x_{j},y_{j})\mid\tau\in\mathcal{T}_{bottom}\}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l10" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">10:</span>
              
              
            Perform one epoch of KTO updates using <math id="alg1.l10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{D}_{pos},\mathcal{D}_{neg}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{D}_{pos},\mathcal{D}_{neg}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l11" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">11:</span>
              
              
            <span id="alg1.l11.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">return</span> <math id="alg1.l11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>π</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
</div>
</figure>
<figure id="alg2" class="ltx_float ltx_float_algorithm ltx_framed ltx_framed_top">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_float"><span id="alg2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Algorithm 2</span> </span> SFT Optimization in our human-AI interaction environment</figcaption>
<div id="alg2.4" class="ltx_listing ltx_framed ltx_framed_topbottom ltx_listing">
<div id="alg2.l1" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">1:</span>
              
              
            <span id="alg2.l1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Input:</span> Initial LLM policy <math id="alg2.l1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>π</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{0}</annotation></semantics></math>, reward model <math id="alg2.l1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>R</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R</annotation></semantics></math> (i.e. user feedback), number of trajectories <math id="alg2.l1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>N</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N</annotation></semantics></math>, selection value <math id="alg2.l1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg2.l2" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">2:</span>
              
              
            <span id="alg2.l2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Output:</span> Optimized LLM policy <math id="alg2.l2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>π</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg2.l3" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">3:</span>
              
              
            Sample <math id="alg2.l3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>N</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N</annotation></semantics></math> conversation trajectories <math id="alg2.l3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau_{1},\ldots,\tau_{N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>τ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>N</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau_{1},\ldots,\tau_{N}</annotation></semantics></math> using <math id="alg2.l3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>π</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{0}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg2.l4" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">4:</span>
              
              
            Score trajectories based on user feedback for each message: <math id="alg2.l4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{R}_{i}=R(\tau_{i})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>R</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{R}_{i}=R(\tau_{i})</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="alg2.l4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i=1,\ldots,N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i=1,\ldots,N</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg2.l5" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">5:</span>
              
              
            Select top trajectories <math id="alg2.l5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{T}_{top}=\{\tau_{i}\mid\hat{R}_{i}&gt;R(\tau_{k})\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>R</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{T}_{top}=\{\tau_{i}\mid\hat{R}_{i}&gt;R(\tau_{k})\}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg2.l6" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">6:</span>
              
              
            Extract training pairs <math id="alg2.l6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(x_{j},y_{j})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(x_{j},y_{j})</annotation></semantics></math> from selected trajectories (each <math id="alg2.l6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y_{j}</annotation></semantics></math> is an agent response, <math id="alg2.l6.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{j}</annotation></semantics></math> contains conversation history up to that point):

</div>
<div id="alg2.l7" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">7:</span>
              
              
            <math id="alg2.l7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{D}=\{(x_{j},y_{j})\mid\tau\in\mathcal{T}_{top}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{D}=\{(x_{j},y_{j})\mid\tau\in\mathcal{T}_{top}\}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg2.l8" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">8:</span>
              
              
